#. type: Content of: <div><h1>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:5
msgid "Hint Submission"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h2>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:6
msgid "How to write a hint"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:8
msgid ""
"A good hint provides information which is not otherwise easily "
"obtainable. In general, we're not interested in hints which copy "
"information already in LFS or BLFS or hints which simply list the "
"steps needed for installing a package as explained in the INSTALL or "
"README of a package."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:14
msgid ""
"This still leaves a broad scope of subjects. Hints can be about "
"anything for which a non-obvious or non-trivial fix or hack is "
"required.  A hint can also explain a complicated package installation "
"or a particular setup.  Have a look at some <a "
"href=\"read.html\">other hints</a> to get an idea of what a hint may "
"include.  Also check out the <a href=\"adoptahint.html\">Adopt a hint "
"program</a> in case there is some cute little hint that you would "
"like to nurture or if someone has suggested a topic for a hint that "
"you have knowledge about."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:23
msgid ""
"Once you have a good idea for a hint, you can start writing. Stick to "
"the following style rules if you want to submit it for inclusion."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h2>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:26
msgid "Submission guidelines"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:29
msgid ""
"Before submitting a hint, check if there is an already existing hint "
"on the topic. If there is then contact the author if you have any "
"updates. If the previous author is not interested in maintaining the "
"hint, or if there is no response from the author for at least a "
"month, then you may take over maintenance of the hint. Remember to CC "
"blfs-dev@lists.linuxfromscratch.org regarding all correspondence with "
"the author so that the hint maintainers are aware of the changeover."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:36
msgid ""
"<i>Note that this does not mean that duplicate hints on the same "
"topic are not allowed.  If you feel that the current author has a "
"different approach to a problem and you have one which does not match "
"the current hint, feel free to submit a separate hint. We suggest "
"communicating with the current author(s) before writing the hint. We "
"suggest writing a short blurb on how the new hint differs from the "
"existing one.</i>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:44
msgid ""
"Hints should be reserved for things that cannot be included into the "
"book. Hints that relate to installation of packages and which would "
"easily fit into the book (usually the BLFS book) should be submitted "
"to the relevant development list. If you are conversant with docbook "
"and XML, then feel free to submit a patch to the current development "
"version of the relevant book..  If not, submit a text file matching "
"the current format of the book and a book editor will do the "
"necessary modifications."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:53
msgid ""
"If you are in the process of writing a hint on a topic, it would be "
"good to drop a line to the relevant list in case someone else is "
"working on something similar."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:57
msgid ""
"A hint should not duplicate documentation that is already available "
"elsewhere on a particular topic. It should complement it. "
"Documentation available elsewhere includes <a href=\"http://"
"www.tldp.org/\">LDP documentation</a>, and documentation available "
"from the package website, documentation available by a simple <a "
"href=\"https://www.google.com/\">google search</a>. Also, things that "
"are already well documented in the book(s) or at the LDP should not "
"be repeated in the hint unless the hint describes matters in more "
"detail, in a different way, or from a different perspective. So "
"things such as installation of db, freetype, zlib, etc can just be "
"referenced by pointers to the book."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:69
msgid ""
"Authors who are not interested in maintaining their hints any more "
"should send a message to the appropriate mailing list specifying that "
"the hint is <a href=\"adoptahint.html\">up for adoption</a>. The "
"author should also notify the hints list if the hint is not relevant "
"anymore."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:75
msgid ""
"Hints that have been integrated into the book will be retired after a "
"stable version of the book is released."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:78
msgid ""
"Keep the file name of the hint short, but descriptive. The extension "
"for the hint should be .txt. The name may be composed of a "
"combination of lowercase letters, numbers, and a few symbols _ - +."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:82
msgid ""
"The hint document is text based. The format for the hints is as "
"explained at the end of this document."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:85
msgid ""
"Avoid including scripts and patches in the hints. Keep these as "
"separate files to avoid spoiling the beauty of the hint.  :)  Patches "
"should follow the <a href=\"/patches/\">patches format</a>. The "
"patches that you submit will be committed to the patches repository "
"(so be sure to mention the hint in the patch description) under the "
"appropriate package name. The scripts or patches that don't fit into "
"the patches project will be available from the <a href=\"downloads/"
"attachments/\">Attachments</a> link on the <a "
"href=\"download.html\">download page</a>.  If you need to reference "
"any patches in your hint, point to the patches subproject (e.g.  "
"http://www.linuxfromscratch.org/patches/&lt;package_name&gt;/"
"&lt;patch_name&gt;).  If you need to reference to any attachments, "
"point to the attachments directory (e.g.  http://"
"www.linuxfromscratch.org/hints/downloads/attachments/"
"&lt;hint_name&gt;/)  Don't worry if the URIs are incorrect, the "
"maintainer will modify the URIs before submitting.  Since maintainers "
"are sometimes lazy, you may need to give them a bit of a push/shove "
"to \"do the right thing\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:103
msgid ""
"To submit or update a hint, send an e-mail to the <a href=\"https://"
"lists.linuxfromscratch.org/sympa/info/blfs-dev\">blfs-dev mailing "
"list</a>. From there it will be picked up by the hint maintainer, who "
"will update the hint index and the tarball. You must be subscribed to "
"the list to post a message to avoid spam on the list."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:110
msgid ""
"<em>Note that by submitting a hint, you agree to the conditions "
"mentioned on this page with respect to the hint. In particular, you "
"allow other users to take over the maintainership of the hint if "
"another user contacts you with a request (for taking over the "
"maintainership or integrating his/her work in your hint) and you fail "
"to respond to the request for a month. If you would not like someone "
"to take over the maintainership of the hint, please state so clearly "
"in the hint.  Authors should also keep the contact information "
"updated.</em>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h2>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:120
msgid "Hint Format"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:122
msgid ""
"Every hint should have the following sections, <i>in the order "
"specified here</i> so as to have a consistent look and feel.  "
"Sections that are supposed to be single lines should be on the same "
"line as the section header. Sections that are more than one line "
"should begin from the line following the header. Check out the <a "
"href=\"sample-hint.txt\">example hint</a> to get an idea about the "
"format."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h3>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:130
msgid "AUTHOR:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:132
msgid ""
"This field can be repeated if there are multiple authors. Each author "
"line should have name and contact details of the hint author.  "
"Restrict this field for the current authors of the hint. Previous "
"authors should be acknowledged in the ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h3>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:137
msgid "DATE:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:139
msgid ""
"The date the hint was last updated in international format (YYYY-MM-"
"DD)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h3>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:142
msgid "LICENSE:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:144
msgid ""
"The license under which the hint is licensed. The hint maintainers "
"suggest the GNU Free Documentation License, but you are free to "
"choose your own. The GNU Free Documentation License allows copying of "
"your hint and modifying it without restriction, with the exception "
"that you will always be credited as author. It also indicates that "
"the hint carries no guarantees. For more information on various "
"licenses, visit the <a href=\"https://www.gnu.org/philosophy/license-"
"list.html\">GNU website</a>.  Before submitting the hint, verify that "
"a copy of the LICENSE under which your hint is licensed is available "
"in the <a href=\"downloads/files/LICENSES/\">LICENSES directory</a>.  "
"If not, at the time of submission of the hint, also include a note "
"and a URI for the hint maintainer to download a text copy of the "
"LICENSE."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h3>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:157
msgid "SYNOPSIS:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:159
msgid ""
"A one line description about the hint. Please keep this short and "
"sweet and restrict it to a single line since this is the title that "
"would be included on the hints page."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h3>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:163
msgid "PRIMARY URI:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:165
msgid ""
"This is an optional section for authors who like to host their own "
"hints and only submit occasional updates to the LFS hints site."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h3>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:169
msgid "DESCRIPTION:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:171
msgid ""
"A short description on why the hint was written, who is the target "
"audience, etc. This would help a user in determining whether the hint "
"is useful for her/him."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h3>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:175
msgid "ATTACHMENTS:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:177
msgid ""
"Links to additional downloads such as patches, scripts, config files, "
"etc. This section is optional."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h3>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:180
msgid "PREREQUISITES:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:182
msgid ""
"In this section list the pre-requisites that the user needs to be "
"aware of before following the hint.  This section can be used to "
"indicate if the hint is applicable only for a particular LFS version."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h3>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:187
msgid "HINT:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:189
msgid ""
"This is the heart of the hint. List the details about your hint here. "
"There is no restriction on how you format things in this section, "
"except (there is always some exception) to avoid lines that look like "
"a section (i.e. Text in all UPPERCASE followed by a semi-colon). "
"Also, make your best effort to restrict each line to 80 columns "
"(though this can be relaxed on case-by-case basis). Avoid including "
"material that is already in the book."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h3>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:197
msgid "ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:199
msgid ""
"Acknowledgements for people who have contributed to the hint. This "
"section is optional."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h3>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:200
msgid "CHANGELOG:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:202
msgid ""
"Include timestamped changes that have occurred in the hint. Add "
"latest entries at the end. Entries in this section should be as "
"follows:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:207
msgid "[YYYY-MM-DD]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:208
msgid "&nbsp;*&nbsp;Changed A"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><ul><li>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:209
msgid "&nbsp;*&nbsp;Changed B"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h2>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:212
msgid "NOTE:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/hints/howtowrite.html:214
msgid ""
"These instructions are based on responses from many users.  If you "
"have suggestions for improving this document, feel free to discuss it "
"on the blfs-dev mailing list."
msgstr ""
